### Description of change

Per https://github.com/sequelize/sequelize/issues/9421 this takes the proposed `indexHints` API and implements it for mysql.

```js
Project.findAll({
  indexHints: [
    { type: IndexHints.USE, values: ['index_project_on_name'] }
  ],
  where: {
    id: {
      [Op.gt]: 623
    },
    name: {
      [Op.like]: 'Foo %'
    }
  }
})
```

Will generate a mysql query that looks like this:

```sql
SELECT * FROM Project USE INDEX (index_project_on_name) WHERE name LIKE 'FOO %' AND id > 623;
```
